-- title:
--   Postprocess H Restriction To Vertical Line Eq Evaluate At
-- statement:
--   **Evaluating a vertical restriction recovers the original polynomial evaluation.**
--
--   Let `params` have a field model, let $H$ be a polynomial-valued submeasurement on the successor space, and let $u\in\mathbb{F}_q^{m+1}$. Restrict each polynomial outcome to the vertical line through the truncated point of $u$, then evaluate the line polynomial at the final coordinate. The result is direct evaluation at $u$:
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{postprocess}\left(\operatorname{hRestrictionToVerticalLine}(\mathrm{params},H,\operatorname{truncatePoint}(u)),f\mapsto f(\operatorname{pointHeight}(u))\right)=\operatorname{evaluateAt}(\mathrm{params.next},u,H).
--   $$
--
--   The point at the indicated height on the vertical line is exactly $u$. This identity is used when line consistency is converted into point consistency.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.postprocess_hRestrictionToVerticalLine_eq_evaluateAt`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
